WD IDE drives have three jumper settings: "Single", Master, and Slave.  Make
sure the jumper settings are correct.

>
>I don't nearly know enough about HDD logic, but I would like to try to swap
>the PCB. I will attempt to source one locally (Melbourne, Australia). If I
>do change the PCB, should I expect the partition information to be intact
>and the drive readable, or is grasping too hard on the straws?

If the PCB has failed and you replace it with an identical PCB, the odds are
extremely good that everything on the drive will be readable.  If the hard drive
heads have crashed and caused a PCB failure, you're out of luck with typical
end-user or dealer hardware tools.

