>With detpm-m I'd have to keep the decxm-m in place; sounds like over
>kill.

BNC to thinwire requires either an Ethernet "Media Converter" which
is very expensive, or a small Ethernet Hub with a few 10BaseT (RJ45)
connectors and a 10Base2 (BNC) connector.  Hubs are cheap, but you
will need to find one that is a couple of years old, built before
they started economizing by leaving off the BNC connector.

Upon re-reading this, I don't know whether this is what you really
want, because I don't know where the BNC to AUI (really AUI to BNC)
transceiver is attached.  If it is on the VAX in question, just take
it off and replace it with an AUI to 10BaseT transceiver.

