I would LOVE to have a VAXstation 3100 -- they were the systems on which I
first learned Ixian incantations and lore, at university. I wasn't even a CS
student, but I signed up for an account on the campus system, and got one.
(I had heard they were for the use of any student,and it turns out it was
true.) I decided that I liked Ultrix pretty well in fairly short order; I
mean, I had absolutely no experience with any form of Unix. All I had to
trade on was my knowledge of my own AmigaDOS, which bears a very faint
resemblance to Unix, but not much.

Anyway, I learned from scratch on Ultrix, and so I got attached to it. Then,
the university began switching from the VAXstations to HP PA-RISC
workstations running HP-UX. It was at this point that I began to appreciate
the small differences that differentiate the various Unices. I decided that
I didn't like HP-UX very much, mostly because I had to change a lot of term
settings, via stty, to get my Amiga's term program to work correctly with
it. Ultrix worked right out of the gate.

Enough jabbering from me. :)




