We had RA81's with PDP-11/70 and VAX 11/750s back in the early '80's,
'82 to '84 timeframe.

In the mid- to late-80's, I had a MicroVAX-II Q5 with an RA81.

In the late 80's, I had number of RA81's on a VAX 8350 cluster, and kept
them when that went to a stand-alone VAX 6000-410. We upgraded those to
RA92's when we needed more capacity, and upgraded the entire storage
subsystem to DSSI when we got pressed for through-put. The DSSI
conversion improved performance so much it almost stopped a -410 to -610
upgrade, except that we needed to up the memory as well.

