The VMS Freeware CD (V5) has media for the DS300.

> 3) How do you configure this beast?  I seem to remember you can do some of
> it from a terminal attached to port 1.

By default port 1 is the console port: it prints all boot time messages. You
can hook up a VTxxx
and login using any username you like. Then SET PRIV  and use the password
SYSTEM.
Then you are a privileged user and you can modify server and port
attributes. DEFINE puts them in NVRAM
and SET modifies the run time values.

Alternatively, if you have access to a system with DECnet (phase IV) then
you can
MC NCP CONNECT NODE DS300
Provided you configured node ds300 in the NCP database:

MC NCP DEFINE NODE 1.1023 NAME DS300 SERVICE CIRC xxx-0 HARDW ADDRE
08-00-2B-hh-hh-hh

Hans
