The VAX 9000, code name Aquarius, was to be a water cooled machine. During
the development of the special logic carriers in Kanata, it was found that
heat removal from the system could be comfortably done strictly on the basis
of conduction though the metal frames of the logic carriers.

The AlphaServer 2100 in fact has an airplane wing in it for cooling the
memory interface logic chips, the upside down plastic wing being
substantially cheaper and easier to refit than a metal heatsink on a custom
packaged chip.

