FWIW...

I now have the ability to scan any current (or past) SPL (fka "ConDist")
for VAX or Alpha and produce CD images (LD containers) for the layered
products licensed under the hobbyist program.

It's written in DCL and it's fairly simple, if a bit time consuming: you
must scan each SPL issue twice, all CDs: once to assemble the list of
products and the required disk space, then invoke a second proc. to add
up the space, figure out how many CD images (LD containers) to build and
assign products to their target images, and then scan the SPL again to
copy the products to the CD images (LD containers) once the images have
been built.

The [CDROM] directory and its contents are not provided on the target
images, however. This may be fixed in a future version, if I can dig up
some data on how to build the CD_CONTENTS.DAT file.

I'll consider putting this code up on my freeware site depending what
kind of feedback I get from this post.

