>Core? or memory? I can't remember ever hearing of Core memory on a
>Vax.  Or 3rd party core for a 11/70. CDC and Memorex did 11/70 memory
>boxes, I have a CDC, and I'd guess Memorex may have done 780 memories
>as well.

Core was synonymous with main storage for many years. When I built my
first computer, an IMSAI 8080 with 4 Seal 8K memory boards, one of
my friends in DP asked me how much core it had and I automatically
answered, "32K".

At a computer club to which I belonged, door prizes were being given
away. This was just after the Apple ][ was introduced. Someone put an
apple on the prize table. The MC announced that they were giving away
an apple and it came with core. Amid groans from the audience, some wag
called out, "How many bites?"
