Antonio:

> DECStation 500/25 what kind of ram and hard disk do i need?

5000/25 is ancient (and pretty darn slow at 25mhz) RISK machine A.K.A.
"Maxine".  It will run VMS, Ultrix, some flavors of Linux, NetBSD, Won't
run any Windoze products.
RAM: 72 Pin, 70ns, True Parity FPM
HD: SCSI2, most DEC RZ series, i.e., RZ24, RZ25, RZ26, etc., probably
maxes out at 4 gb (don't know for sure), other brands will work, Seagate
DSP series and the like.

> 1 decstation 3000/300
> what kind of hard disk and ram is needed?

It's an Alpha AXP (DEC 21064 "EV4", 64 bit processor), A.K.A.
"Pelican",  Depending on model (L vs. LX), processor speed can be either
125 or 175mhz.
OS's: OpenVMS, UNIX (and variants), some flavors of Linux (?), NetBSD.
Wont run Windoze products at all.
RAM: 72 Pin, 70nx, True Parity FPM
HD: SCSI2, DEC RZ series, Seagate DSP, etc.

Of the two, spend your time and money on the 3000/300.

Good computing!

Tom



