not had to re-install, though I did apply service packs as they appeared.
The only time I had a serious problem I was able to use the Vulcan
Salute to bring up Task Manager and use Backup to restore to my most
recent backup.

> What is the exact configuration you use on your machine?  What
> hard drives?  IDE or SCSI?  Is your CDrom a master or slave?

	It came with a 2 GB Quantum drive rebadged as Digital, a
Matsushita (I think) rebadged again, and a Digital SCSI DAT tape.  The
SCSI controller is QLogic and I'm led to believe that this early in
the production cycle I cannot use external SCSI devices.  I've added
a Maxtor 5 GB drive and another IDE CD drive that I bought in Silicon
Valley many years ago (got caught smuggling the Maxtor into ZRH and
overcharged in import duty because the customs thought the invoice
was in Sterling rather than $US; I'd flown in via LHR after riding
a motorcycle up to SF and catching a connection to LAX from Oakland...
-- I'd been up over 48 hours and didn't spot the mistake.)

> I'd like to try again to have mine work.

	I found the software with a relatively easy google search[1].
First step is to download the latest firmware and reprogram the EEPROMS.
Then download a diskette's worth of HAL definitions and another with
the latest IDE drivers -- both are needed when loading the OS.  As I
said, the disk must be set up with a small FAT partition and the
OS partition must also be FAT initially (can change to NTFS during or
after instillation) -- you can get the default 6 MB FAT + the rest FAT
(possibly divided up in 4 GB chunks) by the default in the AlphaBIOS's
Hard Disk utility.

